WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.940
In 1928, the Soviet Union began running
its economy through five-year plans.

2
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:10.240
Officials set output targets
for factories and fixed prices.

3
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.880
In 1978, China began market reforms.

4
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:18.580
Farm households were soon allowed to
sell output above their state quota.

5
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.090
So who really decides what gets made:

6
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.030
prices, planners, or a mix?

7
00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:28.580
In this mission, you'll meet the three
questions every economy must answer:

8
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.320
what, how and for whom.

9
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.110
Then you'll compare free market,

10
00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:38.380
planned and mixed economies, and
see why every real economy is mixed.

11
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:42.470
Your mission: explain how each
system answers those questions,

12
00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.360
and weigh up what each does well.
